le/annual-2024.txt-282-part on such ownership, the Company relies primarily on the innovative skills, technical competence and marketing abilities of its personnel.\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-283-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-284-The Company regularly files patent, design, copyright and trademark applications to protect innovations arising from its research, development, design and\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:285:marketing, and is currently pursuing thousands of applications around the world. Over time, the Company has accumulated a large portfolio of issued and\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-286-registered intellectual property rights around the world. No single intellectual property right is solely responsible for protecting the Company’s products and\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-287-services. The Company believes the duration of its intellectual property rights is adequate relative to the expected lives of its products and services.\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-288-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-289-In addition to Company-owned intellectual property, many of the Company’s products and services are designed to include intellectual property owned by third\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-290-parties. It may be necessary in the future to seek or renew licenses relating to various aspects of the Company’s products, processes and services. While the\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-291-Company has generally been able to obtain such licenses on commercially reasonable terms in the past, there is no guarantee that such licenses could be\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-292-obtained in the future on reasonable terms or at all.\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-293-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-294-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-295-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-296-                                                                   Apple Inc. | 2024 Form 10-K | 3\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-297-\fBusiness Seasonality and Product Introductions\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-298-The Company has historically experienced higher net sales in its first quarter compared to other quarters in its fiscal year due in part to seasonal holiday\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-299-demand. Additionally, new product and service introductions can significantly impact net sales, cost of sales and operating expenses. The timing of product\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-300-introductions can also impact the Company’s net sales to its indirect distribution channels as these channels are filled with new inventory following a product\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-301-launch, and channel inventory of an older product often declines as the launch of a newer product approaches. Net sales can also be affected when consumers\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-302-and distributors anticipate a product introduction.\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-303-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-304-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-305-Human Capital\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-306-The Company believes that its people play an important role in its success, and strives to attract, develop and retain the best talent. The Company works to\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-307-create an inclusive, safe and supportive environment for all of its team members, so that its people can do the best work of their lives. As of September 28, 2024,\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-308-the Company had approximately 164,000 full-time equivalent employees.\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-309-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-310-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-311-Compensation and Benefits\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-312-The Company believes that compensation should be competitive and equitable, and should enable employees to share in the Company’s success. The\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-313-Company recognizes its people are most likely to thrive when they have the resources to meet their needs and the time and support to succeed in their\n--\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-1095-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-1096-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-1097-Purchases of Equity Securities by the Issuer and Affiliated Purchasers\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:1098:Share repurchase activity during the three months ended September 28, 2024 was as follows (in millions, except number of shares, which are reflected in\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt:1099:thousands, and per-share amounts):\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-1100-                                                                                                                              Total Number of              Approximate Dollar\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-1101-                                                                                                                                  Shares                        Value of\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-1102-                                                                                                                             Purchased as Part           Shares That May Yet Be\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-1103-                                                                             Total Number             Average Price             of Publicly                    Purchased\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-1104-                                                                               of Shares                Paid Per            Announced Plans or             Under the Plans or\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-1105-Periods                                                                       Purchased                  