design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-2305-the 2022 Plan generally vest over four years, based on continued employment, and are settled upon vesting in shares of the Company’s common stock on a\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-2306-one-for-one basis. All RSUs granted under the 2022 Plan have dividend equivalent rights, which entitle holders of RSUs to the same dividend value per share as\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-2307-holders of common stock. A maximum of approximately 1.3 billion shares were authorized for issuance pursuant to 2022 Plan awards at the time the plan was\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-2308-approved on March 4, 2022.\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-2309-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-2310-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-2311-2014 Employee Stock Plan\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-2312-The Apple Inc. 2014 Employee Stock Plan, as amended and restated (the “2014 Plan”), is a shareholder-approved plan that provided for broad-based equity\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-2313-grants to employees, including executive officers. The 2014 Plan permitted the granting of the same types of equity awards with substantially the same terms as\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-2314-the 2022 Plan. The 2014 Plan also permitted the granting of cash bonus awards. In the third quarter of 2022, the Company terminated the authority to grant new\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-2315-awards under the 2014 Plan.\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-2316-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-2317-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-2318-\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-2319-                                                                 Apple Inc. | 2024 Form 10-K | 44\n--\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-2321-A summary of the Company’s RSU activity and related information for 2024, 2023 and 2022, is as follows:\ndocs/design/cases/apple/annual-2024.txt-232